  "verbalization": "Propylamine is implicated in a complex network of interactions leading to ME-180 through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Propylamine acts as a target for several entities, with NCI-H1650 being a common intermediate in these relationships. NCI-H1650 is a target of Arnebifuranone and a related compound, both of which are linked to ME-180. This indicates that Propylamine may influence ME-180 through the metabolic or enzymatic pathways involving these compounds. Additionally, Propylamine is linked to a dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase, which is a target of another compound that also targets ME-180. This suggests that Propylamine may exert its effects through a broader cellular mechanism, possibly involving protein kinase inhibition or other signaling pathways. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Propylamine and ME-180, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
